{"step_index":309,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:13:07Z","thinking":"The previous run likely timed out due to the NXDOMAIN status reported by both Google and Cloudflare DoH, potentially indicating a propagation delay or caching issue with the TXT record. The presence of the old, residual TXT record in BIND before the run supports this hypothesis, as it might have interfered with the validation process. Now, the Domain's status is showing NXDOMAIN.\n\n\nThe validation failure likely stems from the caching of the old TXT record by Google and Cloudflare DNS resolvers, which had a TTL of 180 seconds, longer than the validation loop. This led to the resolvers returning the old value, even after the new value was set, causing the consecutive check to fail. Modifying the zone update script to set a shorter TTL (e.g., 60 seconds) for the `_acme-challenge` record should mitigate this.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"ssh ns1 'echo -e \"\\$TTL 180\\n@ IN SOA ns1.outremer-telecom.fr. noc.resot.net. ( 2026100201 12H 2H 4W 3H )\\n NS ns1.outremer-telecom.fr.\\n_acme-challenge.geo 60 TXT \\\"test\\\"\" > /tmp/testzone && named-checkzone sfrcaraibe.fr /tmp/testzone'","Cwd":"/home/koby/LINUX","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing zone syntax with 60s TTL","toolSummary":"Checking 60s TTL syntax with named-checkzone"}}]}
